%% CONTROL for rule 3, and the witness for the _is_horizontal predicate.
%% Seven nodes in a TB graph is a tall diagram, not a wide one, and rule 3 is about width: the
%% 900px cap scales a wide picture DOWN and a narrow one UP, so the two shapes need different
%% advice. Force _is_horizontal to True and this file starts firing.
%% EXPECT: none | - — baseline only. No pattern owns this file; the predicate does.
graph TB
  t1["one"] --> t2["two"] --> t3["three"] --> t4["four"] --> t5["five"] --> t6["six"] --> t7["seven"]
